extraction_notes: |
  - Read from Dragons and Gods printed 34-36 (the species entry), 17 (the Dragon Experience Table) and 50 (Hatchling Dragon as an optional Player Character), each number read off a page render because the text layer carries the digit cipher (206 for 2D6, 406 for 4D6, 1 04x l 0 for 1D4x10).
  - SHAPE COPIED FROM chiang-ku-dragon: a hatchling variant and an adult variant carrying attribute dice, pools, horror factor and bonuses; everything else shared. The top-level skills, magic and psionics describe the HATCHLING, because printed 50 makes the hatchling the player character and a variant cannot override `magic` or `psionics`. The adult''s psionics and magic are recorded as special abilities.
  - xp_table is the shared Dragon Experience Table, printed 17: the lower bound of each of levels 1-15. Printed 50 says to use it for a hatchling player character.
  - starting_money 0 and no equipment: printed 50, "start with no possessions".
  - "+N on all other saving throws" is written out as fourteen save keys, the gargoyle-lord convention: every save the sheet draws except horror_factor (stated separately) and coma_death_pct (a percentage).
  - Hatchling skills: languages and basic math start at 96%, advanced math and all other skills at first level proficiency (catalog base plus the printed bonus). The adult variant restates the named 98% skills; the two language choice groups cannot be overridden by a variant and stay at the hatchling''s 96%.
  - "Literate in Dragonese/Elven and four other languages ... plus speaks six ADDITIONAL languages" is read as ten spoken languages (the four it reads plus six) and five literacies. Language: Dragonese is granted because the page names the literacy and the six spoken languages are called additional.
  - Scholar/Technical is the catalog''s Technical category. The +10% applies to the category selections. The page''s "Include I.Q. bonus (if any) to all skills" is the general rule and is not encoded per skill.
  - The hatchling''s spells are dice-valued (1D4+4 at first level, 1D4+1 at each even level to 14), which `spells_starting` and `spells_schedule` cannot hold, so the magic block states the gate (air is a warlock elemental tradition, levels 1-3) and no count; the counts are in special_abilities. The warlock tradition also holds Earth, Fire and Water spells - the page allows AIR only, and the player honours that.
  - Rifts conversion block (printed 36) omitted, as chiang-ku omits its own.
  - Average adult level (1D6+6), habitat, life span, enemies and allies are lore, recorded below.
